<title>POLAND: Warta falls 5.8 pct on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Warta falls 5.8 pct on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Polish insurance company Warta SA fell 5.8 percent to 56.5 zlotys in 1.0-million zloty turnover on profit-taking after surging 20 percent since September 6, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's definitely profit-taking,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Warta kept rising since September 6, but it experienced an even more significant surge since September 9, after news was released that it had received a tax refund of 12.8 million zlotys. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
